From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:35:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Skip host regions whole when looking for a free area
 on macOS.

map_free_area() looks for room between Wine's views, and
try_map_free_area() steps through each gap one allocation granularity
(64 KB) at a time, with one fixed mach_vm_map per step. On macOS, much of
the address space belongs to the host without being a view: dyld's shared
cache, the loader's and the host libraries' allocations, the 3 GB the
system reserves under the top of the address space, a 385 GB guard region
under 0x7000000000. Each of those costs one failed mach_vm_map per 64 KB.
Every thread's stack and thread data below 4 GB walked ~2,960 failed
probes through a 185 MB host range above 0x100230000, each process start
walked 3,567 through the reserved area at the top, and once the first
gaps fill, a thread's allocation walks the guard region: ~7.2 million
failed probes, ~1.2 s per thread. A benchmark creating threads made 500
in 0.36 s and then only 478 more in 600 s; SMITE 2's engine took 31-97 s
to initialise, against 16 s under the x86_64 Wine on Rosetta.

When a fixed mapping fails because the range is occupied, ask
mach_vm_region() for the first region at or above the candidate. If it
overlaps the candidate, every candidate up to its end (bottom-up) or down
to its start minus the size (top-down) overlaps it too, so continue from
there, aligned as before. Otherwise step as before. The [base, end) limits
are still checked by the loop. Only candidates that would have failed are
skipped, so the result is the address the stepping would have found
(unless the host maps or unmaps concurrently, as before). Nothing changes
off macOS; map_free_area() is try_map_free_area()'s only caller.

Local to MacNeutron; not proposed upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 750eefe2..a52430c5 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1258,6 +1258,48 @@ static struct wine_rb_entry *find_view_inside_range( void **base_ptr, void **end
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           skip_host_region
+ *
+ * After a fixed mapping of [start, start + size) failed, return the next
+ * candidate past the host region in the way: the first one at or above
+ * start, which Wine doesn't track as a view (dyld's shared cache, the
+ * loader's and the host libraries' allocations). Bottom-up, its end rounded
+ * up; top-down, its start minus size rounded down: every candidate in
+ * between overlaps it. Returns start + step if no region overlaps.
+ */
+static void *skip_host_region( void *start, size_t size, ptrdiff_t step )
+{
+    size_t align_mask = (step > 0 ? step : -step) - 1;
+    mach_vm_address_t address = (mach_vm_address_t)start, next;
+    mach_vm_size_t region_size;
+    vm_region_basic_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count = VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_COUNT_64;
+    mach_port_t dummy_object_name = MACH_PORT_NULL;
+
+    if (mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &address, &region_size, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
+                        (vm_region_info_t)&info, &count, &dummy_object_name ) ||
+        address >= (mach_vm_address_t)start + size)
+        return (char *)start + step;
+
+    if (step > 0)
+    {
+        next = (address + region_size + align_mask) & ~(mach_vm_address_t)align_mask;
+        if (next <= (mach_vm_address_t)start) return NULL;  /* wrapped */
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        if (address < size) return NULL;
+        next = (address - size) & ~(mach_vm_address_t)align_mask;
+    }
+    TRACE( "skipping host region %p-%p, next %p.\n", (void *)address,
+           (void *)(address + region_size), (void *)next );
+    return (void *)next;
+}
+#endif
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           try_map_free_area
  *
@@ -1281,7 +1323,13 @@ static void* try_map_free_area( void *base, void *end, ptrdiff_t step,
             (step < 0 && (char *)start - (char *)base < -step) ||
             step == 0)
             break;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        /* one fixed mach_vm_map per granularity step through a host region
+         * of gigabytes costs seconds: skip it whole */
+        start = skip_host_region( start, size, step );
+#else
         start = (char *)start + step;
+#endif
     }
 
     return NULL;
-- 
